01:16:27.440 --> 01:16:27.840
Yes.

01:16:28.040 --> 01:16:29.320
I hope that's not as big as...

01:16:29.320 --> 01:16:30.260
No, I don't know.

01:16:30.640 --> 01:16:32.360
You use your own judgment.

01:16:32.560 --> 01:16:37.780
I'm not going to tell you how much or how little because I'm not going to fall into the trap, all right?

01:16:38.380 --> 01:16:38.780
Yes.

01:16:39.340 --> 01:16:40.800
Does the wine have to be red wine?

01:16:41.260 --> 01:16:43.680
No, about the wine.

01:16:43.920 --> 01:16:47.140
Does it have to be red?

01:16:47.700 --> 01:16:52.000
There's one Rabbi, the Ramban, who says it has to be red.

01:16:52.300 --> 01:16:54.600
But all of the other rabbis, they disagree,

01:16:55.100 --> 01:16:57.380
and they say it could be white,

01:16:57.380 --> 01:17:01.020
it could be any wine that you like.

01:17:01.620 --> 01:17:02.660
It could be champagne.

01:17:03.080 --> 01:17:06.900
Champagne, according to Jewish law, it is real wine.

01:17:07.480 --> 01:17:09.520
So champagne is Kashel LePesach,

01:17:09.880 --> 01:17:12.360
and you could use it for this.

01:17:12.360 --> 01:17:16.420
Now, there is only one Rabbi, the Ramban, who says it has to be red,

01:17:16.980 --> 01:17:19.680
and therefore, according to Ramban, champagne is not good because it's white.

01:17:20.080 --> 01:17:23.680
But many other rabbis disagree with the Ramban and say,

01:17:23.800 --> 01:17:29.180
no, you drink whatever wine is more pleasant for you.

01:17:30.420 --> 01:17:34.580
Now, of course, you know, I mean, it's a question of taste.

01:17:35.480 --> 01:17:37.480
But our community follows Ramban.

01:17:38.480 --> 01:17:40.420
No, Ramban, the Ramban, no.

01:17:40.420 --> 01:17:44.980
I tell you why I come here. I come here because my father thought they were poor parents and grandparents and they could buy champagne.

01:17:49.580 --> 01:17:53.300
They could not buy champagne. They used to make the wine at home.

01:17:53.460 --> 01:17:54.880
I don't remember, you know.

01:17:55.200 --> 01:17:58.600
They didn't have no champagne. That's why they followed the other opinion.

01:17:59.100 --> 01:17:59.600
I'm telling you.

01:18:00.520 --> 01:18:01.140
Yes, sir.

01:18:03.260 --> 01:18:06.520
My opinion is, they're going to have to do something.

01:18:06.520 --> 01:18:10.080
The grape juice in America

01:18:10.080 --> 01:18:12.180
I say in my opinion

01:18:12.180 --> 01:18:12.980
Is not good

01:18:12.980 --> 01:18:14.240
And I tell you why

01:18:14.240 --> 01:18:16.440
Because in America

01:18:16.440 --> 01:18:18.760
In order not to pay federal taxes

01:18:18.760 --> 01:18:19.420
For

01:18:19.420 --> 01:18:22.800
Because wine you pay federal taxes

01:18:22.800 --> 01:18:24.200
Alcohol you pay federal taxes

01:18:24.200 --> 01:18:26.760
And then it will cost you more

01:18:26.760 --> 01:18:28.780
So let me tell you

01:18:28.780 --> 01:18:30.620
From the point of view of law

01:18:30.620 --> 01:18:31.440
Of Jewish law

01:18:31.440 --> 01:18:34.760
If you have grape juice

01:18:34.760 --> 01:18:36.060
It's cashier for Pesah

01:18:36.060 --> 01:18:37.680
Why?

01:18:38.340 --> 01:18:39.520
Green grape juice

01:18:39.520 --> 01:18:42.780
Because as soon as you squeeze it

01:18:42.780 --> 01:18:45.100
And comes in contact with air

01:18:45.100 --> 01:18:47.620
The process of fermentation begins

01:18:47.620 --> 01:18:49.200
Alright?

01:18:50.040 --> 01:18:52.640
And therefore it's kosher

01:18:52.640 --> 01:18:54.960
However in America

01:18:54.960 --> 01:18:59.060
In order to prevent that the grape juice ever would go into ferment

01:18:59.060 --> 01:19:02.100
Because then you have to pay the taxes as you pay for that

01:19:02.100 --> 01:19:04.420
They put certain kind of powder or chemical

01:19:04.420 --> 01:19:07.680
that prevents it ever to ferment.

01:19:08.540 --> 01:19:10.560
And therefore, in my opinion, that's my opinion,

01:19:10.700 --> 01:19:14.180
I'm not saying that you're, again, I'm not preaching.

01:19:14.340 --> 01:19:15.920
I'm just teaching you what my opinion is.

01:19:16.320 --> 01:19:19.500
In my opinion, grape juice is not good.

01:19:19.760 --> 01:19:26.320
However, there are grape juice in Israel that they sell in America.

01:19:26.320 --> 01:19:27.620
I think it's called tirosh.

01:19:28.560 --> 01:19:28.920
Yes?

01:19:29.160 --> 01:19:31.380
And they have this, which is kosher.

01:19:31.820 --> 01:19:33.620
You could buy the tirosh if you don't like it.

01:19:33.620 --> 01:19:41.280
you know, you buy it in any Jewish wine store, and I think that the tirosh, it's good because it's written,

01:19:41.720 --> 01:19:45.540
yes, how much time do I have? All right, all right.

01:19:46.100 --> 01:19:47.580
Tirosh, which I think is good.

01:19:48.160 --> 01:19:52.240
Now, for kids, obviously, it doesn't have to be real wine.

01:19:52.340 --> 01:19:57.040
You could buy them regular kosher grape juice.

01:19:57.040 --> 01:19:58.320
It's all right because that's for kids.

01:19:58.600 --> 01:20:03.100
They don't have to be so meticulous for kids.

01:20:03.100 --> 01:20:08.880
That's alright, whatever it is

01:20:08.880 --> 01:20:10.800
Yeah, but whatever it is

01:20:10.800 --> 01:20:12.960
But if the kids want grape juice

01:20:12.960 --> 01:20:15.300
Give them grape juice, there's no need for kids

01:20:15.300 --> 01:20:16.280
You know, but

01:20:16.280 --> 01:20:19.320
You could mix the wine

01:20:19.320 --> 01:20:20.240
But

01:20:20.240 --> 01:20:22.820
It should not be diluted in the sense that it

01:20:22.820 --> 01:20:24.380
It's alcoholic

01:20:24.380 --> 01:20:27.880
You could put a little bit of water

01:20:27.880 --> 01:20:29.160
Certainly, of course

01:20:29.160 --> 01:20:32.100
Now, one point

01:20:32.100 --> 01:20:42.400
about two more points and then I'll let you take over. Two points. Now, we're going to talk about dessert.

01:20:43.600 --> 01:20:54.040
Very important. The word afikoman is a Greek word which means dessert. What you have always for dessert?

01:20:54.040 --> 01:20:56.640
the thing that you like best

01:20:56.640 --> 01:20:57.820
yes

01:20:57.820 --> 01:20:59.440
ice cream

01:20:59.440 --> 01:21:01.340
I don't know

01:21:01.340 --> 01:21:02.780
strawberries with

01:21:02.780 --> 01:21:05.540
with cream

01:21:05.540 --> 01:21:07.420
I don't know

01:21:07.420 --> 01:21:10.260
French pastries

01:21:10.260 --> 01:21:11.240
alright

01:21:11.240 --> 01:21:13.160
but

01:21:13.160 --> 01:21:15.440
since this is Pesah

01:21:15.440 --> 01:21:17.840
for us the thing we love more

01:21:17.840 --> 01:21:20.320
is the Massah

01:21:20.320 --> 01:21:22.520
and therefore

01:21:22.520 --> 01:21:25.540
the afikoman is the last thing that we eat.

01:21:25.580 --> 01:21:26.680
You could eat the sherbet,

01:21:27.040 --> 01:21:28.300
and you could eat this and that,

01:21:28.780 --> 01:21:31.760
but the afikoman should be the last thing that you eat.

01:21:32.360 --> 01:21:33.500
After you eat it,

01:21:34.260 --> 01:21:35.160
you say birkat amazon,

01:21:36.340 --> 01:21:38.680
and then comes the second,

01:21:39.180 --> 01:21:40.400
the last part of the serer,

01:21:41.180 --> 01:21:42.540
in which you're only saying,

01:21:43.020 --> 01:21:44.420
thank you, thank you, thank you God,

01:21:44.580 --> 01:21:45.900
thank you, thank you, thank you God.

01:21:46.440 --> 01:21:48.360
And this is one glass of wine,

01:21:48.980 --> 01:21:49.860
borefiyak gefen,

01:21:49.860 --> 01:21:51.620
and then you begin with the hallelujah,

01:21:51.620 --> 01:21:53.180
Yod, Nishmat Kol Chai,

01:21:53.500 --> 01:21:54.780
and all of this are

01:21:54.780 --> 01:21:57.480
thank you to God. Thank you, thank you,

01:21:57.580 --> 01:21:59.460
thank you, thank you. And when you finish

01:21:59.460 --> 01:22:01.480
thank you, say, let it be that the

01:22:01.480 --> 01:22:03.320
next year there should be, the temple

01:22:03.320 --> 01:22:05.460
should be built, and we should be able to bring

01:22:05.460 --> 01:22:07.500
the actual Qorban Pesah, and we should

01:22:07.500 --> 01:22:08.760
be able to say to you

01:22:08.760 --> 01:22:11.220
all our prayers in Jerusalem.

01:22:11.720 --> 01:22:13.540
Don't forget, we began

01:22:13.540 --> 01:22:13.820
with

01:22:13.820 --> 01:22:19.760
and we finished

01:22:19.760 --> 01:22:21.320
wishing that really

01:22:21.320 --> 01:22:25.100
next year we should be the bed I mean as we should be built and we should be a

01:22:25.100 --> 01:22:31.520
list and then you drink the fourth glass of wine and that's it so therefore just

01:22:31.520 --> 01:22:45.940
look imagine a meal a formal meal yes which is we have a theme we want all the

01:22:45.940 --> 01:22:51.220
people in the [inaudible] table to participate as the aggada

01:22:51.220 --> 01:22:57.180
everybody participates we eat together every food has a symbolic meaning

01:22:57.180 --> 01:23:04.360
Masa, Maror, the Zeroha, the egg, Zekh le Hagiga and so on everything is and the

01:23:04.360 --> 01:23:15.440
people will will interact yes and then after the meal we take a cognac and a

01:23:15.440 --> 01:23:22.900
a Vanasigar, and we sit down by the library, nice fireplace,

01:23:23.580 --> 01:23:27.220
and we sing songs and say, thank you, God.

01:23:27.500 --> 01:23:29.160
It's beautiful to be Jewish.

01:23:30.040 --> 01:23:31.060
We love you.

01:23:31.800 --> 01:23:32.260
That's all.

01:23:32.940 --> 01:23:34.980
We're just all of us singing together.

01:23:35.340 --> 01:23:36.160
This is the hallelujah.

01:23:36.980 --> 01:23:37.460
Clear?

01:23:38.040 --> 01:23:38.460
All right?

01:23:40.280 --> 01:23:40.640
Discussion?

01:23:40.860 --> 01:23:41.740
One minute.

01:23:42.580 --> 01:23:42.860
Yes.

01:23:43.280 --> 01:23:43.580
Harry.

